          "email": "johgras@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-02 21:25:47.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21099 build: pass WQ_PERCPU to per-CPU workqueues",
        "message": "LU-21099 build: pass WQ_PERCPU to per-CPU workqueues\n\nLinux 7.2 warns, with a stack trace, when alloc_workqueue() is given\nneither WQ_PERCPU nor WQ_UNBOUND, then sets WQ_PERCPU itself:\n\n  workqueue: cfs_rh is using neither WQ_PERCPU or WQ_UNBOUND.\n  Setting WQ_PERCPU.\n  WARNING: kernel/workqueue.c:5851 at __alloc_workqueue+0x468/0x4d0\n\nThis fires on every obdclass load, and panics hosts running with\npanic_on_warn.\n\nPass WQ_PERCPU explicitly to the cfs_rh, kfilnd_wq, gss_cleanup_wq\nand osd-ldiskfs integrityd workqueues, which were already per-CPU by\ndefault, so behaviour is unchanged. Add a configure check for\nWQ_PERCPU and define it as 0 on older kernels.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: John Grasso <johgras@amazon.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I276820b68efeef0053b2c475fd795031aa1182f9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
